<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales up 0.7 pct--BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales up 0.7 pct--BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 0.7 percent in the week ended June 7 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 3.1 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index slipped 0.3 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;The abnormal cool weather pattern clearly has hurt demand for apparel, horticulture, and air conditioners, which have posted weak sales in April and May,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
